    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nThe audit output confirms the new format working end-to-end:\n```\nAUDIT - owner created id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1 ...\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSW2716E6609E1\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n`NSW` (region) + `27` (FY) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**New/changed logic**\n- **`AssignOwnerMemberId`** (new, replaces `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` + `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`): computes `REGION` (from postcode), `FY` (2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date), `HASH8` (first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`), and `CHK` (single Luhn digit over the digits of `REGION+FY+HASH8`), concatenates them, and applies collision handling (`-<n>` suffix) to the `memberId`.\n- **`Owner`**: removed `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields and `getCheckDigit()`; added `memberId` (`member_id` column). `getLocality()` now derives the region from the `memberId`'s leading letters, and `getFiscalYear()` from the `memberId`'s FY segment \u2014 so the fiscal-year value and owner segment (via locality) all reference the `memberId`.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** / **`AuditOwnerCreated`**: the structured audit record and the human-readable line now carry `memberId`.\n\n**Wiring & schema**\n- `owners.POST.yml`: the two assign steps collapsed into one `assignMemberId` step.\n- `openapi.yml`: replaced the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` schemas with `memberId`, removed `checkDigit`, and updated the `fiscalYear`/`locality` descriptions (the generated `OwnerDto` + MapStruct auto-map the renamed property).\n- All four DB schemas (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`): `customer_code` + `membership_number` columns replaced by a single `member_id`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` passes, and nothing else references the removed fields.",
