    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe refactor is a coherent, well-executed consolidation that matches how this codebase is already structured.\n\n- **Right unit / no catch-all:** Collapsing `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` + `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` into a single `AssignOwnerMemberId` is exactly what \"unify into one memberId\" calls for \u2014 the two former steps existed only because there were two ids. The new class assembles one value from region + FY + HASH8 + CHK; every private helper (`sha256Hex8`, `deduplicate`, `luhnCheckDigit`) contributes to that single responsibility, so it reads as cohesive identity-assembly, not a grab-bag. It follows the existing `Assign<E>` naming and the pre-existing `sha256Hex8`/`deduplicate` idiom.\n- **Logic moved to the correct place:** The Luhn computation correctly migrated from a response-time `Owner.getCheckDigit()` getter into assignment time, since CHK is now baked into `memberId` at creation rather than re-derived on read. Removing the standalone getter is the right call.\n- **Derived getters stay consistent:** `getLocality()` and `getFiscalYear()` continue the codebase's existing pattern of parsing the primary id at response time (previously they parsed `customerCode`); `getFiscalYear()` reusing `getLocality().length()` as the segment offset is a reasonable, minimal coupling and remains robust to the `-<n>` dedup suffix.\n- **Additive coherence across layers:** Model field, both derived getters, the audit line, `OwnerCreatedEvent` (including the now-obsolete migration note being replaced), all four schema dialects, the POST pipeline YAML, and the OpenAPI schema are all updated in lockstep. Javadoc is thorough and cross-references are kept accurate.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find this natural. No structural changes needed.",
